cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this methodological code, please cite both the article and this repository."
title: "Methodological code: The impact of the Canterbury earthquakes on household income and expenditure in the Canterbury region in New Zealand"
type: software
abstract: "Methodological R code accompanying the accepted Natural Hazards and Earth System Sciences article on household income and expenditure after the Canterbury earthquakes. The archive documents the harmonisation of Household Economic Survey variables, residence classification, earthquake-intensity assignment, propensity-score matching, difference-in-differences estimation, heterogeneity analysis, robustness checks, and output construction. Restricted-data components are intended for use within the controlled Stats NZ Integrated Data Infrastructure environment by researchers approved for the relevant project and in accordance with Stats NZ requirements."
